---
# The agent's name, lowercase — every harness offers it as `<plugin>:<name>`
# (`{PLUGIN_NAME}:{AGENT_NAME}`), and a subdirectory under `agents/` joins
# the label too: `agents/review/security.md` is `{PLUGIN_NAME}:review:security`.
name: {AGENT_NAME}

# What the model reads when it decides to hand work to this agent: say when
# to use it, not what it is. Keep it double-quoted: in plain text a `: `
# breaks the value and ` #` starts a comment.
description: {AGENT_DESCRIPTION}

# `name` and `description` are what every harness reads the same way.
# Anything else (a model, a tool list) is one harness's own vocabulary:
# the harness that reads it keeps it, and every other one is delivered the
# agent without it — the install names what each one did not receive.
---
Replace this with the agent's instructions, in the order it acts on them:
what it reads first, what it does, and what it must never do. Everything
below the closing `---` is the agent's prompt.
